# Intent: On-unit timers and alarms, device side: a saved schedule (NVS namespace mp_timers) ticked by the stackchan task off the RTC-backed clock, so a timer rings with no host and after a reboot. A due timer shows the reminder card with a happy face, pulses the ring cyan, plays the notification sound every 8 s unless silent, keeps the screen awake, and pushes timer_fired and timer_ended events to the host (new device_events_push; event extras are now copied, not borrowed). A ring ends by itself after one minute. The stop word is not armed in this base.
# Placement: unit (the schedule must keep running with the host down)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/hal.cpp, hal_mcp.cpp, board/stackchan.cc, board/hal_bridge.h; new hal/maipai_timers.cc and .h, hal/device_events.h (MIT)
